From d0ae2ba4527c3e29783d7f9668d26601135dba88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:19:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: reconstruct a Dolby Vision picture for output as
 HDR10

The renderer of the bridge reconstructs a Dolby Vision picture (the
base layer, the residual of the enhancement layer, the reshaping and
the colour matrices of the RPU) into BT.2020 PQ, and from there packs
it into the transport of native output. For a display that takes HDR10
and not Dolby Vision, the reconstruction itself is the picture: this
adds a way to have it, with no transport and no tone mapping.

dvbridge_render_hdr10() draws the picture, or a part of it, at its
place in a floating-point texture of the size of the output. What a
frame is drawn with is what the composed way of native output draws
with (the same libplacebo parameters, the same clamp to [0, 1]); the
target is the picture's own colour space, so that nothing is mapped. A
renderer made for this (dvbridge_renderer_create_hdr10()) does not have
the 3840x2160 texture of native output. A frame that is refused before
anything of it is drawn (its metadata does not hold, its place does not
fit) leaves the one before it in the texture; when the draw itself
fails, the texture holds no whole picture until the next one is drawn
(dvbridge_render_hdr10_last() says which).

dvbridge_gl_copy() copies that texture into a framebuffer of the same
size, sample for sample: the window. A fixed-point framebuffer gets the
nearest of its levels, which the shader picks, 1/256 of a step above
the level; a floating-point one gets the values as they are. It can
write the limited range of an RGB signal, as Kodi's video does when its
output is set to that.

The picture is reconstructed in the middle of a frame that the caller
goes on drawing: Kodi draws its GUI over the video afterwards.
dvbridge_gl_state_save() and dvbridge_gl_state_restore() keep the GL
state it does that with around a reconstruction and around the set-up
of a renderer, which both leave libplacebo's state behind: program,
vertex array, array buffer, the two framebuffers, viewport, scissor,
blending, colour mask, unpack alignment, nine capabilities, and the 2D
texture and the sampler of the first sixteen units (libplacebo binds
the textures of a pass to the units from 0 on and leaves them unbound:
seven for a picture with an enhancement layer). dvbridge_gl_copy() does
so by itself.

dvbridge_hdr10_static() gives what an HDR10 output is told of such a
picture: the luminance of the mastering display and the light levels of
level 6 of the RPU when it has one, as they are (the brightest pixel may
be above the peak of the mastering display, as in any HDR10 stream;
only what cannot be a light level is left out: more than 10000 cd/m2,
or a frame average above a brightest pixel that is given), and
otherwise the range of the source that the RPU states, with no light
levels. Every value fits the 16 bits it has in the infoframe.

Drawn by a software renderer (zink on lavapipe) from a FEL stream, in
36 and 12 drawings: the picture is the one of the composed way of
native output inside the active area, sample for sample (0.0000 codes
of 1023 apart); copied to a 10-bit framebuffer, every sample is the
nearest code, whole and in part, with the first row at the top and at
the bottom, in the full and the limited range (64 copies), nothing is
written outside the rectangle and the scissor is as it was; copied to
a half-float framebuffer the values are within 2^-11; a part of the
picture drawn alone is within one code of the same part of the whole
(0.50 at most: the chroma samples are filtered from other positions);
a frame that is refused leaves the picture before it.

And as Kodi uses it: a renderer made for HDR10 alone gives the same
picture, value for value; copied into the default framebuffer (what a
window is: 3840x2160, 10 bits) with the first row at the bottom and in
the limited range, whole and between two bars, every sample is the
nearest code (16 copies); and of 40 values of GL state that a caller
had set, other framebuffers, a scissor rectangle, blending and a
texture on each of four units among them, a reconstruction changed 9
to 11, all of which were put back. The static metadata of the test
stream reads 4000 and 0.0050 cd/m2, MaxCLL 3991, MaxFALL 2363, and the
rules above are checked with its level 6 block and source range
changed.

Three things of that renderer are why it is written as it is. Its copy
of one framebuffer to another (glBlitFramebuffer) cut values off
instead of rounding them; it makes 10 bits of a float by dropping six
of 16, so that a level written 1/64 of a step above its value came out
one too high from 1015 on; and a half-float texture as the intermediate
cut the reconstruction off by up to half a code, which is why the
intermediate has 32 bits.
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.c | 197 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.h |  32 +++++
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_placebo.c |  38 ++++++
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_placebo.h |  13 ++
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c  | 148 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.h  |  26 ++++
 6 files changed, 452 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.c
index 34ecddf..23fee63 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.c
@@ -78,6 +78,203 @@ void dvbridge_gl_packer_destroy(struct dvbridge_gl_packer *p)
     free(p);
 }
 
+struct dvbridge_gl_copier {
+    GLuint program, vao, sampler;
+    GLint picture, flip_height, levels, limited;
+};
+
+static const char COPY_VERTEX[] =
+    "#version 300 es\n"
+    "void main()\n"
+    "{\n"
+    "    vec2 position = vec2((gl_VertexID << 1) & 2, gl_VertexID & 2);\n"
+    "    gl_Position = vec4(position * 2.0 - 1.0, 0.0, 1.0);\n"
+    "}\n";
+
+/* levels: the highest code of a fixed-point target of up to 12 bits; 0.0 for a floating-point
+ * one, and for more bits than a float keeps apart, which get the values as they are. The level
+ * is written 1/256 of a step above its value. A framebuffer that rounds what it is given makes
+ * that level of it, and so does one that cuts it off, also the one that makes 10 bits by
+ * dropping six of 16, whose steps are a little narrower (a software renderer does that: written
+ * 1/64 of a step above their value, the levels from 1015 on came out one too high there). */
+static const char COPY_FRAGMENT[] =
+    "#version 300 es\n"
+    "precision highp float;\n"
+    "uniform highp sampler2D picture;\n"
+    "uniform int flip_height;\n"
+    "uniform float levels;\n"
+    "uniform int limited;\n"
+    "out vec4 color;\n"
+    "void main()\n"
+    "{\n"
+    "    ivec2 p = ivec2(gl_FragCoord.xy);\n"
+    "    if (flip_height > 0)\n"
+    "        p.y = flip_height - 1 - p.y;\n"
+    "    vec3 c = clamp(texelFetch(picture, p, 0).rgb, 0.0, 1.0);\n"
+    "    if (limited != 0)\n"
+    "        c = (c * 876.0 + 64.0) / 1023.0;\n"
+    "    if (levels > 0.0)\n"
+    "        c = (floor(c * levels + 0.5) + 0.00390625) / levels;\n"
+    "    color = vec4(c, 1.0);\n"
+    "}\n";
+
+struct dvbridge_gl_copier *dvbridge_gl_copier_create(void)
+{
+    GLuint vs = compile(GL_VERTEX_SHADER, COPY_VERTEX);
+    GLuint fs = compile(GL_FRAGMENT_SHADER, COPY_FRAGMENT);
+    struct dvbridge_gl_copier *c = vs && fs ? calloc(1, sizeof(*c)) : NULL;
+    if (!c) {
+        glDeleteShader(vs);
+        glDeleteShader(fs);
+        return NULL;
+    }
+    c->program = glCreateProgram();
+    glAttachShader(c->program, vs);
+    glAttachShader(c->program, fs);
+    glLinkProgram(c->program);
+    glDeleteShader(vs);
+    glDeleteShader(fs);
+    GLint linked;
+    glGetProgramiv(c->program, GL_LINK_STATUS, &linked);
+    c->picture = glGetUniformLocation(c->program, "picture");
+    c->flip_height = glGetUniformLocation(c->program, "flip_height");
+    c->levels = glGetUniformLocation(c->program, "levels");
+    c->limited = glGetUniformLocation(c->program, "limited");
+    if (!linked || c->picture < 0 || c->flip_height < 0 || c->levels < 0 || c->limited < 0) {
+        dvbridge_gl_copier_destroy(c);
+        return NULL;
+    }
+    glGenVertexArrays(1, &c->vao);
+    glGenSamplers(1, &c->sampler);
+    glSamplerParameteri(c->sampler, GL_TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, GL_NEAREST);
+    glSamplerParameteri(c->sampler, GL_TEXTURE_MAG_FILTER, GL_NEAREST);
+    glSamplerParameteri(c->sampler, GL_TEXTURE_WRAP_S, GL_CLAMP_TO_EDGE);
+    glSamplerParameteri(c->sampler, GL_TEXTURE_WRAP_T, GL_CLAMP_TO_EDGE);
+    return c;
+}
+
+void dvbridge_gl_copier_destroy(struct dvbridge_gl_copier *c)
+{
+    if (!c)
+        return;
+    glDeleteVertexArrays(1, &c->vao);
+    glDeleteSamplers(1, &c->sampler);
+    glDeleteProgram(c->program);
+    free(c);
+}
+
+static const GLenum STATE_CAPS[] = {GL_BLEND, GL_DEPTH_TEST, GL_STENCIL_TEST, GL_SCISSOR_TEST,
+    GL_DITHER, GL_CULL_FACE, GL_RASTERIZER_DISCARD, GL_SAMPLE_ALPHA_TO_COVERAGE,
+    GL_SAMPLE_COVERAGE};
+_Static_assert(sizeof(STATE_CAPS) / sizeof(*STATE_CAPS) ==
+                   sizeof(((struct dvbridge_gl_state *)0)->enabled),
+               "one flag for each capability");
+
+void dvbridge_gl_state_save(struct dvbridge_gl_state *s)
+{
+    GLboolean mask[4];
+    glGetIntegerv(GL_CURRENT_PROGRAM, &s->program);
+    glGetIntegerv(GL_VERTEX_ARRAY_BINDING, &s->vertex_array);
+    glGetIntegerv(GL_ARRAY_BUFFER_BINDING, &s->array_buffer);
+    glGetIntegerv(GL_DRAW_FRAMEBUFFER_BINDING, &s->draw_framebuffer);
+    glGetIntegerv(GL_READ_FRAMEBUFFER_BINDING, &s->read_framebuffer);
+    glGetIntegerv(GL_VIEWPORT, s->viewport);
+    glGetIntegerv(GL_SCISSOR_BOX, s->scissor);
+    glGetIntegerv(GL_BLEND_SRC_RGB, &s->blend[0]);
+    glGetIntegerv(GL_BLEND_DST_RGB, &s->blend[1]);
+    glGetIntegerv(GL_BLEND_SRC_ALPHA, &s->blend[2]);
+    glGetIntegerv(GL_BLEND_DST_ALPHA, &s->blend[3]);
+    glGetIntegerv(GL_UNPACK_ALIGNMENT, &s->unpack_alignment);
+    glGetBooleanv(GL_COLOR_WRITEMASK, mask);
+    for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i)
+        s->mask[i] = mask[i];
+    glGetIntegerv(GL_ACTIVE_TEXTURE, &s->active_texture);
+    for (int unit = 0; unit < DVBRIDGE_GL_STATE_UNITS; ++unit) {
+        glActiveTexture(GL_TEXTURE0 + unit);
+        glGetIntegerv(GL_TEXTURE_BINDING_2D, &s->texture[unit]);
+        glGetIntegerv(GL_SAMPLER_BINDING, &s->sampler[unit]);
+    }
+    glActiveTexture(s->active_texture);
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof(STATE_CAPS) / sizeof(*STATE_CAPS); ++i)
+        s->enabled[i] = glIsEnabled(STATE_CAPS[i]);
+}
+
+void dvbridge_gl_state_restore(const struct dvbridge_gl_state *s)
+{
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof(STATE_CAPS) / sizeof(*STATE_CAPS); ++i) {
+        if (s->enabled[i])
+            glEnable(STATE_CAPS[i]);
+        else
+            glDisable(STATE_CAPS[i]);
+    }
+    for (int unit = 0; unit < DVBRIDGE_GL_STATE_UNITS; ++unit) {
+        glActiveTexture(GL_TEXTURE0 + unit);
+        glBindTexture(GL_TEXTURE_2D, s->texture[unit]);
+        glBindSampler(unit, s->sampler[unit]);
+    }
+    glActiveTexture(s->active_texture);
+    glColorMask(s->mask[0], s->mask[1], s->mask[2], s->mask[3]);
+    glBlendFuncSeparate(s->blend[0], s->blend[1], s->blend[2], s->blend[3]);
+    glPixelStorei(GL_UNPACK_ALIGNMENT, s->unpack_alignment);
+    glScissor(s->scissor[0], s->scissor[1], s->scissor[2], s->scissor[3]);
+    glViewport(s->viewport[0], s->viewport[1], s->viewport[2], s->viewport[3]);
+    glBindFramebuffer(GL_DRAW_FRAMEBUFFER, s->draw_framebuffer);
+    glBindFramebuffer(GL_READ_FRAMEBUFFER, s->read_framebuffer);
+    glBindVertexArray(s->vertex_array);
+    glBindBuffer(GL_ARRAY_BUFFER, s->array_buffer);
+    glUseProgram(s->program);
+}
+
+bool dvbridge_gl_copy(struct dvbridge_gl_copier *c, unsigned texture, unsigned framebuffer,
+                     int width, int height, int x, int y, int w, int h, bool flip, bool limited)
+{
+    if (!c || !texture || width < 1 || height < 1 || w < 1 || h < 1 || x < 0 || y < 0 ||
+        x > width - w || y > height - h)
+        return false;
+    for (int i = 0; i < 16 && glGetError() != GL_NO_ERROR; ++i)
+        ;
+    struct dvbridge_gl_state state;
+    dvbridge_gl_state_save(&state);
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof(STATE_CAPS) / sizeof(*STATE_CAPS); ++i)
+        glDisable(STATE_CAPS[i]);
+    glActiveTexture(GL_TEXTURE0);
+    bool ok = false;
+    glBindFramebuffer(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, framebuffer);
+    /* what the framebuffer holds: fixed-point levels, or floating-point values */
+    const GLenum attachment = framebuffer ? GL_COLOR_ATTACHMENT0 : GL_BACK;
+    GLint red = 0, green = 0, blue = 0, samples = 0, type = 0, encoding = 0;
+    glGetIntegerv(GL_RED_BITS, &red);
+    glGetIntegerv(GL_GREEN_BITS, &green);
+    glGetIntegerv(GL_BLUE_BITS, &blue);
+    glGetIntegerv(GL_SAMPLES, &samples);
+    glGetFramebufferAttachmentParameteriv(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, attachment,
+        GL_FRAMEBUFFER_ATTACHMENT_COMPONENT_TYPE, &type);
+    glGetFramebufferAttachmentParameteriv(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, attachment,
+        GL_FRAMEBUFFER_ATTACHMENT_COLOR_ENCODING, &encoding);
+    const bool floating = type == GL_FLOAT;
+    if (glCheckFramebufferStatus(GL_FRAMEBUFFER) != GL_FRAMEBUFFER_COMPLETE || glGetError() ||
+        (!floating && type != GL_UNSIGNED_NORMALIZED) || red != green || red != blue ||
+        red < 8 || red > 16 || samples > 1 || encoding != GL_LINEAR)
+        goto restore;
+    glViewport(0, 0, width, height);
+    glEnable(GL_SCISSOR_TEST);
+    glScissor(x, flip ? height - y - h : y, w, h);
+    glColorMask(GL_TRUE, GL_TRUE, GL_TRUE, GL_TRUE);
+    glUseProgram(c->program);
+    glBindVertexArray(c->vao);
+    glBindSampler(0, c->sampler);
+    glBindTexture(GL_TEXTURE_2D, texture);
+    glUniform1i(c->picture, 0);
+    glUniform1i(c->flip_height, flip ? height : 0);
+    glUniform1f(c->levels, floating || red > 12 ? 0.0f : (float)((1u << red) - 1));
+    glUniform1i(c->limited, limited);
+    glDrawArrays(GL_TRIANGLES, 0, 3);
+    ok = glGetError() == GL_NO_ERROR;
+restore:
+    dvbridge_gl_state_restore(&state);
+    return ok && glGetError() == GL_NO_ERROR;
+}
+
 bool dvbridge_gl_pack(struct dvbridge_gl_packer *p, unsigned texture, unsigned framebuffer,
                      int width, int height, const uint32_t packets[512], unsigned count, bool flip)
 {
diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.h b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.h
index 8e2c015..a3f57c3 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.h
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.h
@@ -11,4 +11,36 @@ void dvbridge_gl_packer_destroy(struct dvbridge_gl_packer *packer);
 bool dvbridge_gl_pack(struct dvbridge_gl_packer *packer, unsigned pq_texture,
                      unsigned framebuffer, int width, int height,
                      const uint32_t packets[512], unsigned count, bool flip_y);
+/* Hades: copies a picture from a float texture (first row at the top) into a framebuffer of the
+ * same size, sample for sample, for output as HDR10. A fixed-point framebuffer gets the nearest
+ * of its levels of every value: the shader picks the level, since a framebuffer may also cut a
+ * value off (a software renderer's copy of one framebuffer to another did). A floating-point one
+ * gets the values as they are. Only the rectangle given (from the top left) is written.
+ * flip_y: the first row of the framebuffer is the bottom one, as in a window. limited: the
+ * values go into the limited range of an RGB signal (64 to 940 of 1023), as those of Kodi's
+ * video do when its output is set to that. The GL state is put back. */
+struct dvbridge_gl_copier;
+struct dvbridge_gl_copier *dvbridge_gl_copier_create(void);
+void dvbridge_gl_copier_destroy(struct dvbridge_gl_copier *copier);
+bool dvbridge_gl_copy(struct dvbridge_gl_copier *copier, unsigned texture, unsigned framebuffer,
+                     int width, int height, int x, int y, int w, int h, bool flip_y,
+                     bool limited);
+/* Hades: the GL state that a caller goes on drawing with when a picture is reconstructed in the
+ * middle of its frame, as it is for output as HDR10: Kodi draws its GUI over the video
+ * afterwards, with client-side vertex arrays and the viewport of the window. libplacebo leaves
+ * its own state (dvbridge_render_hdr10(), and the first use of a pl_opengl). Saved before and
+ * restored after; dvbridge_gl_copy() does the same by itself. The 2D texture and the sampler of
+ * the first texture units are among it: libplacebo binds the textures of a pass to the units
+ * from 0 on and leaves them unbound (seven of them for a picture with an enhancement layer). */
+#define DVBRIDGE_GL_STATE_UNITS 16
+struct dvbridge_gl_state {
+    int program, vertex_array, array_buffer, draw_framebuffer, read_framebuffer;
+    int viewport[4], scissor[4], blend[4];
+    int unpack_alignment, active_texture;
+    int texture[DVBRIDGE_GL_STATE_UNITS], sampler[DVBRIDGE_GL_STATE_UNITS]; /* 2D, by unit */
+    unsigned char mask[4];
+    unsigned char enabled[9];
+};
+void dvbridge_gl_state_save(struct dvbridge_gl_state *state);
+void dvbridge_gl_state_restore(const struct dvbridge_gl_state *state);
 #endif
diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_placebo.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_placebo.c
index b1d1a9a..ceeebcf 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_placebo.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_placebo.c
@@ -4,6 +4,44 @@
 #include "dvbridge_metadata.h"
 #include <libplacebo/utils/libav.h>
 
+bool dvbridge_hdr10_static(struct dvbridge_hdr10_static *out, const void *metadata, size_t bytes)
+{
+    if (!out || !metadata || (uintptr_t)metadata % _Alignof(AVDOVIMetadata) ||
+        !dvbridge_dv_bounds(metadata, bytes))
+        return false;
+    *out = (struct dvbridge_hdr10_static){0};
+    const AVDOVIMetadata *m = metadata;
+    const AVDOVIDmData *l6 = av_dovi_find_level(m, 6);
+    if (l6 && l6->l6.max_luminance > 0 && l6->l6.max_luminance <= 10000 &&
+        l6->l6.min_luminance < l6->l6.max_luminance * 10000u) {
+        out->level6 = true;
+        out->max_luminance = l6->l6.max_luminance;
+        out->min_luminance = l6->l6.min_luminance; /* 16 bits in the block */
+        /* The light levels as the block has them, like those of an HDR10 stream: the content may
+         * be brighter than the mastering display says. Only what cannot be a light level is left
+         * out: more than the signal can carry, or a frame average above the brightest pixel.
+         * Either may be 0, not known, with the other one given. */
+        if (l6->l6.max_cll <= 10000) {
+            out->max_cll = l6->l6.max_cll;
+            if (l6->l6.max_fall <= (l6->l6.max_cll ? l6->l6.max_cll : 10000))
+                out->max_fall = l6->l6.max_fall;
+        }
+        return true;
+    }
+    const AVDOVIColorMetadata *color = av_dovi_get_color(m);
+    if (color->source_max_pq == 0 || color->source_max_pq > 4095 ||
+        color->source_min_pq >= color->source_max_pq)
+        return false;
+    const float max = pl_hdr_rescale(PL_HDR_PQ, PL_HDR_NITS, color->source_max_pq / 4095.0f);
+    const float min = pl_hdr_rescale(PL_HDR_PQ, PL_HDR_NITS, color->source_min_pq / 4095.0f);
+    if (!(max >= 1) || max > 10000 || !(min >= 0) || min >= max)
+        return false;
+    out->max_luminance = (unsigned)(max + 0.5f);
+    /* a black level above what the field holds (6.5535 cd/m2) is not one a mastering display has */
+    out->min_luminance = min * 10000 + 0.5f < 65535 ? (unsigned)(min * 10000 + 0.5f) : 65535;
+    return true;
+}
+
 bool dvbridge_map_color(struct dvbridge_color *out, const void *metadata,
                        size_t bytes, bool enhancement_layer_paired, bool *residual_omitted)
 {
diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_placebo.h b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_placebo.h
index 1abcb4f..74e41a1 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_placebo.h
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_placebo.h
@@ -11,6 +11,19 @@ struct dvbridge_color {
     struct pl_dovi_metadata dovi;
 };
 
+/* Hades: what an HDR10 output says of a picture reconstructed with this metadata, which is the
+ * picture as it was mastered. From the level 6 block when the metadata has one. Without it, the
+ * luminance range of the source as the metadata gives it, and the light levels not known.
+ * Every value fits the 16 bits it has in the HDMI infoframe. */
+struct dvbridge_hdr10_static {
+    bool level6;            /* taken from a level 6 block */
+    unsigned max_luminance; /* of the mastering display, cd/m2: 1 to 10000 */
+    unsigned min_luminance; /* ... in 0.0001 cd/m2: at most 65535 */
+    unsigned max_cll;       /* cd/m2, at most 10000; 0: not known */
+    unsigned max_fall;      /* cd/m2, at most max_cll when that is known; 0: not known */
+};
+bool dvbridge_hdr10_static(struct dvbridge_hdr10_static *out, const void *metadata, size_t bytes);
+
 /* Output owns its mapping; do not copy it without rebinding repr.dovi.
  * A FEL picture (NLQ active) without its paired enhancement layer is refused, unless
  * residual_omitted is given (Hades): it is then mapped with the base-layer reshaping alone and
diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
index a9f1cb3..fa6c4c1 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
@@ -12,6 +12,10 @@ struct dvbridge_renderer {
     pl_gpu gpu;
     pl_renderer renderer;
     pl_tex rgb;
+    /* Hades: the picture for output as HDR10 (dvbridge_render_hdr10()); whether the last call
+     * drew it, and whether the texture holds a whole picture (that one or an earlier one) */
+    pl_tex hdr10;
+    bool hdr10_ready, hdr10_whole;
     struct dvbridge_context *context;
     struct dvbridge_candidate *pending;
     bool ready;
@@ -165,7 +169,19 @@ static struct pl_hook_res mask_active_area(void *priv, const struct pl_hook_para
     return (struct pl_hook_res){.failed = mask->failed, .output = PL_HOOK_SIG_NONE};
 }
 
+static struct dvbridge_renderer *create_renderer(pl_gpu gpu, pl_log log, bool transport);
+
 struct dvbridge_renderer *dvbridge_renderer_create(pl_gpu gpu, pl_log log)
+{
+    return create_renderer(gpu, log, true);
+}
+
+struct dvbridge_renderer *dvbridge_renderer_create_hdr10(pl_gpu gpu, pl_log log)
+{
+    return create_renderer(gpu, log, false);
+}
+
+static struct dvbridge_renderer *create_renderer(pl_gpu gpu, pl_log log, bool transport)
 {
     if (!gpu)
         return NULL;
@@ -188,10 +204,10 @@ struct dvbridge_renderer *dvbridge_renderer_create(pl_gpu gpu, pl_log log)
     r->context = dvbridge_create();
     pl_fmt fmt = pl_find_fmt(gpu, PL_FMT_FLOAT, 4, 32, 32,
                              PL_FMT_CAP_RENDERABLE | PL_FMT_CAP_SAMPLEABLE);
